Backport of the upstream civetweb fix a87a7aaffd "Modify STOP_FLAG_ASSING to make TSAN happy (#1333)":
https://github.com/civetweb/civetweb/commit/a87a7aaffd

With STOP_FLAG_NEEDS_LOCK, STOP_FLAG_ASSIGN reads the expected value of the compare-and-swap with a plain
(non-atomic) load, which races with the atomic accesses of the stop flag in the other civetweb threads.
This is not in any civetweb release yet (latest is v1.16); remove this patch when we upgrade to a release which contains it.

diff --git a/src/civetweb.c b/src/civetweb.c
--- a/src/civetweb.c
+++ b/src/civetweb.c
@@ -2312,7 +2312,9 @@ STOP_FLAG_ASSIGN(stop_flag_t *f, stop_flag_t v)
 {
 	stop_flag_t sf;
 	do {
-		sf = mg_atomic_compare_and_swap(f, *f, v);
+		sf = mg_atomic_compare_and_swap(f,
+		                                __atomic_load_n(f, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST),
+		                                v);
 	} while (sf != v);
 }
 
